From a7c3098bcc26f42241c65b4d523ce8446c40ddeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:58:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] Option to split the shortwave with the ERA5 direct
 radiation (fdir)

toposcale.direct_diffuse: empirical (default, diffuse fraction from the
clearness index) or era5: the direct radiation on a horizontal surface of
the ERA5 radiation scheme, the diffuse being SW - fdir. get_era5() then
fetches fdir with the surface fields, from the CDS or GDEX. A store keeps
fetching every variable it holds, and a variable added to a stream makes
that stream be fetched again (the other is kept), instead of refusing the
store. The output store records the option.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012FMkEYDUJxvxmd3SbUsJfP
